<header class="masthead">
  {{!-- §6.5/KDV-MOBILE-05: the left cluster owns the flowing content (logo mark,
       species status, nav) and wraps INTERNALLY; the language switcher is its
       SIBLING so it can never leave the mark's row — the masthead itself does not
       wrap. The reflow is content-driven (flex-wrap), with no media/container
       breakpoints. DOM order stays mark, species, nav. --}}
  <div class="masthead-main">
  {{!-- §6.5: inline the trusted logo (triple-stash) — no separate request.
       The <img> is the build-time fallback when the controller supplies no
       logo_svg (e.g. a dataset built without the static tree). --}}
  <a class="mark" href="{{locale_prefix}}/">{{#if logo_svg}}{{{logo_svg}}}{{else}}<img src="/logo.svg" alt="Kodavr" width="32" height="32">{{/if}}</a>
  {{!-- §6.2/§7.13: the species status — a non-interactive status pill next to
       the separate withdraw action. The pill mirrors the stored declaration
       (§6.2); SSR ships both the pill and the link hidden and empty, and
       site.js fills the status text, carries the declaration date as the
       link's title and clears the declaration when the link is followed. No
       role="status": a live region must not wrap an interactive link, and it
       would capture the announce() role fallback. The wrapper is the group
       site.js walks to find the withdraw link (the link stays OUTSIDE the
       pill); `.masthead-main` owns the flowing layout, so the species group
       climbs onto the mark's row only when it fits (demo layout). --}}
  <p class="species-declaration">
    <span class="species-chip" id="species-chip" hidden
       data-machine-label="{{copy.chip_machine_template}}"
       data-human-label="{{copy.chip_human_label}}"
       data-title-template="{{copy.chip_title_template}}"><span class="species-chip-text"></span></span><span class="species-separator" aria-hidden="true">·</span><a class="species-chip-withdraw" href="{{locale_prefix}}/" data-withdraw hidden>{{copy.chip_withdraw_label}}</a>
  </p>
  {{!-- §6.5/KDV-MOBILE-05: a presentational grow-spacer between the cluster and
       the nav. Base size 0, so it never forces a wrap and never changes where the
       line breaks; on the WIDE line it grows and flushes the nav (and everything
       after it on that line) against the language switcher. On a wrapped line the
       spacer stays on the wide line, so the nav alone stays left-aligned — no
       `margin-left:auto` on `.nav`. Inert without JS (no roles, no content). --}}
  <span class="masthead-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  {{!-- §6.6: the nav is data-driven (route datasets carry `nav` with a `current`
       flag rendered as aria-current="page"); the static list is the fallback. --}}
  <nav class="nav" aria-label="{{copy.nav_primary}}">
    {{#if nav}}
    {{#each nav}}
    <a href="{{href}}"{{#if current}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>{{label}}</a>
    {{/each}}
    {{else}}
    <a href="{{locale_prefix}}/">home</a>
    <a href="{{locale_prefix}}/reception/">reception</a>
    <a href="{{locale_prefix}}/about/">about</a>
    <a href="{{locale_prefix}}/contribute/">contribute</a>
    {{/if}}
  </nav>
  </div>
  {{!-- §11/KDV-I18N-06: the language switcher — a native <details>, so it opens
       and closes without JS. The summary shows the current locale's endonym; the
       menu lists every BUILT locale as a link to this SAME page. `aria-current`
       marks the active locale; the hrefs are root-relative and the P2c pass
       relativizes them. site.js closes the menu on outside click / Escape and,
       when the browser prefers another BUILT locale, highlights the switcher with
       an accessible hint (`data-lang-hint` + the summary's name/title) — no
       navigation and no URL/SEO change. Without JS this stays a plain switcher. --}}
  <details class="lang-switch" data-current-locale="{{locale}}" data-lang-hint-template="{{copy.lang_hint}}">
    <summary class="lang-switch-summary" aria-label="{{copy.lang_switch_label}}"><span class="lang-switch-current">{{#each languages}}{{#if current}}{{endonym}}{{/if}}{{/each}}</span></summary>
    <ul class="lang-switch-menu">
      {{#each languages}}
      <li><a href="{{href}}" hreflang="{{hreflang}}" lang="{{hreflang}}" data-lang-code="{{code}}"{{#if current}} aria-current="true"{{/if}}>{{endonym}}</a></li>
      {{/each}}
    </ul>
  </details>
</header>
